  "finalText": "PDB entry 6M0J is the X-ray crystal structure of the SARS-CoV-2 spike receptor-binding domain bound to ACE2. Its resolution is **2.45 Å**.\n\nRCSB lists 2 protein entities for this entry (IDs 1 and 2), and each maps to one UniProtKB accession (SIFTS mapping):\n\n| Entity | Chain | Protein | UniProtKB | Organism (UniProtKB scientific name) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | A | Angiotensin-converting enzyme 2 | Q9BYF1 | Homo sapiens |\n| 2 | E | Spike protein S1 (receptor-binding domain) | P0DTC2 | Severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus 2 |\n\nAll values came from rightclick-x tools: the resolution and entity mappings from RCSB, and the organism names from UniProtKB's own records for these two accessions.\n\nANSWER: 2.45 | Q9BYF1: Homo sapiens; P0DTC2: Severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus 2"
